--- a/lib/Class/Accessor/Inherited/XS.pm
+++ b/lib/Class/Accessor/Inherited/XS.pm
@@ -223,6 +223,13 @@
 
 =head1 PERFORMANCE
 
+On builds with C<PERL_RC_STACK>, including XPerl, opcode optimizations are
+disabled. Accessors use the normal XS call path so Perl can manage stack
+reference counts. This costs the opcode shortcut's performance benefit.
+The C<OPTIMIZED_ENTERSUB> constant reports whether opcode optimization is
+enabled after checking C<CAIXS_DISABLE_ENTERSUB>. C<OPTIMIZED_OPMETHOD>
+reports whether method opcode optimization is available in this build.
+
 L<Class::Accessor::Inherited::XS> is at least 10x times faster than L<Class::Accessor::Grouped>, depending
 on your usage pattern. Inherited accessors have constant speed even in large inheritance chains. Object accessors
 are even faster than L<Class::XSAccessor> ones.
